_file {
    - This file is used for preingestion of ideas into the graph
    - It is for ideas that are being drafted, haven't been placed, haven't been linked or represent a significant superseding descructive change to the graph 
       - i.e. requiring careful integration to leave no trace of deprecated ideas, leave no duplication and leave no conflicts
    - ingestion must pass validation via `pnpm run val` (["../development/core.rq".pnpm_val]: check, test, build)
    - ingestion requires reqiurement integration into the graph, followed by actual implementation if requested.
}

attribute_namespaceing {
    an idea's attributes should be referenceable in links.
    @example {
        my subidea
    }
    
    an idea should be able to access `[attribute_namespacing.example]`
    Links should link appropriately the parser, lexer, ... extension, html...
    @todo
    @implementation
    
}

code-comment-syntax-errors {
    any time a comment line contains `rq:[*]`, or common patterns it should be parsed, and be considered in `reqlan check`...
    @todo
}


idea-leading-whitespace {
    Block ideas often have leading whitespace
    The base level should be decided by the first line, subsequent lines should not be fully trimmed
    THis line has 4 spaces (same as first line). It should parse with no leading whitespace
        This line has 8 spaces (4 more than first line) it should parse with 4 spaces as part of the content.

    @implementation
    @tests
    @todo
}

html-export-changes {
    The print page should be aware of the [idea-leading-whitespace]
    @todo
}

empty-attributes {
    it should be perfectly acceptable to have empty attributes
    e.g.:

    @

    This should not break the parsing of the file. (Including in extension errors as well as parser/lexer/tokenizer errors)

    @todo
}

reqlan-check-glob-patterns {
    When running `reqlan check` it should be possible to specify --glob patterns to check specific files.
    It should be possible to specify multiple glob patterns.
    If the targets are outside of the glob, they should be checked, but, not recursively.

    @todo
    @tests
}


idea-tooltip-file-link-accuracy {
    Superseded by ["../extension/language/syntax/features-syntax-highlighting.rq".traceable_inlay_hints]:
    inbound inlay label `location` and tooltip targets both use the shared goto / document-link URI builder.
    @status done
    @deprecated ["../extension/language/syntax/features-syntax-highlighting.rq".traceable_inlay_hints]
}

code-action-duplication {
    I don't know why, but sometimes, the code action drop down duplicates options until there are many.
    Without just truncating or deduplicating, resolve the explosion.
    @bug
}

markdown-rendering-in-html-export {
    Exported html should fully render any refernced markdown content if reqlan is not expressive enough.
    Including images, tables, katex, mermaid and other markdown extensions
    @status plan and triage
}

scoring-on-depth-basis {
    support for a depth score attribute
    and search weighting on the basis of file depth and idea in file count
    @status plan and triage
}

markdown-to-reqlan-and-markdown-to-markdown-support {
    per title
    @status plan and triage
}

